    "description": "Project Posting: Freelance Technical Writer / Software Documentation Specialist (m/f/d) About the project: We are looking for an experienced freelancer for a period of 2 months to fundamentally restructure our product documentation and to design and write a comprehensive, precise software manual. This role is for someone who understands technical documentation not just as writing, but who can systematically analyze complex software processes, roles, and workflows and translate them into a clear, user-oriented information architecture. Project Details: Start: Immediately Duration: 2 months Workload: Full-time Location: Remote Contract Type: Freelance Your tasks in the project: Within the 2-month sprint, your focus will be on the conception, structuring, and writing of the new software manual and accompanying documents. Conception & Information Architecture: Development of a clear, role-based, and task-oriented structure for the new software manual and the online help. Content creation: Writing and revising user manuals, release documentation, FAQs, and administrator guides for complex software topics (e.g., document management, role/permission concepts, workflows, approvals, and audit trails). Knowledge structuring: Preparing and structuring product knowledge from user stories, functional specifications, Jira tickets, release notes, and direct expert interviews with product owners and developers. Terminology & standards: Establishing and maintaining a binding project terminology for user interfaces, actions, status models, and functional rules to ensure consistent documentation. Your profile: Mindset: You love to delve deeply into complex technical software workflows, structure them logically, and write them up in a way that is easy for users to understand. Experience: Proven project success in creating comprehensive software manuals and technical documentation in B2B or enterprise environments. Technical understanding: Quick grasp of software architectures, user interfaces, permission concepts, and release processes. Methodology: Solid knowledge of modern documentation approaches (e.g., Docs-as-Code, Markdown, structured information capture) as well as experience with version control tools (Git) and collaboration platforms (Jira/Confluence). Domain knowledge (advantageous): Experience in regulated industries (pharmaceuticals, medtech, biotech, quality management, or SOP systems) is a major plus. Languages: Excellent German and very good English for precise, clear, and target-group-oriented writing. What makes the project attractive: Focus on the essentials: You will be responsible for the entire lifecycle of the manual, from initial structuring to the finished text chapter. Clear project framework: A focused, 2-month mandate with clear milestones and direct impact for our users. Professional environment: Close collaboration on equal footing with product owners, development teams, and quality assurance.\n\nSkills: documentation, software, Technical writing, Write",
